        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0329" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1071.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-01T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department’s February 27, 10 p m. Upon further consideration the Department
                    is of the opinion that it would be unwise for you to accompany any commission
                    sent by Bordas to treat with Arias. Therefore you are instructed not to
                    accompany commission but to lend it all aid looking to its proceeding to Puerto
                    Plata, and you are furthermore instructed to confer with the commander of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Petrel</hi> who will have received orders to convey
                    the commission to the north should such a course be considered necessary.</p>
                <p>If the commission is not successful in its mission to arrive at an agreement with
                    Arias, have Commander of the <hi rendition="#italic">Petrel</hi> before
                    returning notify him that you desire his presence in the capital to confer with
                    him upon important matters and that if he should refuse to come at the request
                    of the Government of the United States that that Government will, if necessary,
                    have to consider him as unfriendly to it and will take such appropriate action
                    as is deemed expedient by the President of the United States of America. Arrange
                    with Bordas for safe conduct of Arias in case he visits you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
